Quick overview (one-line)

Use a Snowflake SECRET (basic auth with USERNAME='x-token-auth' and the Bitbucket PAT), an API INTEGRATION (provider git_https_api) that restricts allowed HTTPS prefixes to your Bitbucket URL, then create a GIT REPOSITORY object in Snowflake that points to your Bitbucket repo. After that create/sync a Workspace in Snowsight to pull/push files. 
Snowflake Documentation
+1

Prerequisites & privileges

A Bitbucket personal access token (PAT) for the repo (or a repo access token) — store it somewhere safe. (Bitbucket docs on access tokens). 
Atlassian Support

A Snowflake role with privileges to create secrets and integrations. Creating an API integration requires ACCOUNTADMIN or a role with the CREATE INTEGRATION privilege; secrets require CREATE SECRET (and USAGE on parent DB/schema). Best practice: use ACCOUNTADMIN (or have an admin run the create steps). 
