Common pitfalls & troubleshooting

Wrong username: for Bitbucket the username must be x-token-auth in the secret — if you use anything else cloning/auth will fail. 
Snowflake Documentation

API_ALLOWED_PREFIXES too narrow or too broad: if Snowflake blocks requests because the URL is not in the allowed prefixes you’ll need to adjust them. Check errors and expand to the required prefix. 
Snowflake Documentation

Privileges: ensure the role that creates the integration has CREATE INTEGRATION / ACCOUNTADMIN. Ensure the role that uses the secret/workspace has USAGE on the secret/schema. 
Snowflake Documentation
+1

PAT permissions: ensure the Bitbucket PAT has repo read/write scopes (depending on whether you only need pull or also push). See Bitbucket token docs. 
